[[Image:Clenched human fist.png|thumb|right|A clenched [[fist]].]]
==English==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang}} {{term|beclencan|beclenċan|lang=ang}}, [[causative]] of {{term|clingan||cling|lang=ang}}. Compare {{term|stink|lang=en}} and {{term|stench|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛntʃ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|clench|es}}

# [[tight|Tight]] [[grip]].
# {{engineering}} A seal that is applied to formed thin-wall [[bushings]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|clench|es}}

# To [[squeeze]]; to [[grip]] or hold tightly.
#: ''He '''clenched''' his fist in anger.''

====Synonyms====
* [[clasp]]
* [[clutch]]

====Antonyms====
* [[unclench]]

